{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1530447-how-many-xp-should-a-mortal-get-to-be-at-the-same-level-as-the-starting-splat","id":1530447,"title":"How many XP should a Mortal get to be at the same level as the starting Splat?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-02-10T08:10:07-08:00","id":1530447,"title":"How many XP should a Mortal get to be at the same level as the starting Splat?","content":"1 of the players want be a Mortal with Minor Template, while the other want to be a Hunter, with the rest wanting to play a Werewolf, Vampire, and Beast. How much would XP does a Mortal need before they're equal or at least aren't significantly less powerful than the Major Template?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-10T09:08:17-08:00","id":1530455,"title":"","content":"Like Rabbit said, it doesn't work that way. Personally I would bump both mortal's merit dots up to ten and call it a day, they picked what they wanted to play, being weaker may well be part of the appeal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-10T09:45:10-08:00","id":1530457,"title":"","content":"In addition to the above, the simple fact is that even without bringing minor or microtemplates into the matter, the closest things a mortal can get to the equivalent of supernatural powers without fiat are Merits, and in theory the sky is the limit when it comes to what Merits can give you, because (as demonstrated by microtemplates being a collection of Merits) they're the part of the mechanics it takes the least effort to make stuff up for \u2014 figuring out how many Experiences an effect is worth (and how/if it scales) and what prerequisites each effect warrants are the main variable that isn't the same set of game balance decisions you'd be making for any other sort of power.<br /> <br /> To loosely answer the base question, the Experience value of those elements of the Vampire, (Forsaken) Werewolf, and Beast templates that have a price run the gamut due to the different dynamics of each of those games, but 15-20 Experiences makes the rough numbers match up as far as accounting for Disciplines, Gifts and rites, Atavisms and Nightmares, and bonus Merit dots.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-10T16:33:56-08:00","id":1530500,"title":"","content":"I feel like Mortal Player Character aren't that really far behide from The Splat I mention, sure, they aren't that powerful on their own, but they don't have the baggage of maintain the need to Hunt, or Feast, and they aren't being hunted down by Spirit/Strix/Heros, they are still human enough that their worldview isn't totally inhuman, and some Human only Merit are just better than some of the Exculsive Power that other Splat get.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-02T04:52:40-07:00","id":1533477,"title":"","content":"A bit of a necro, but I would like to throw my 2 cents about this.<br /> <br /> As others said before, I would probably give at least 10 merits at the start (or 3xp as Hunter the Vigil did). Now about the power, I think that can vary a lot based on what you consider power, if that's about combat prowess? Social? mystery solving? You see, you would need a completely different skill set for each one, and that's fine. Mortals, have a big disadvantage, of not innately having these powers, but if your players are picking a minor template (not sure if you mean like a ghoul or from hurt locker template, but I believe it is Hurt Locker), you could give some additional free dots related to the template that grab his attention, but I wouldn't go past 5xp, and would call it a day. I you really want it, you could go for xp equality, for instance, a vampire receive 3 disciplines as start, maybe give the player something like 10~15xp, to make up for the blood potency and disciplines he didn't got (2 in-clan, 1 outside), If I remember it right, werewolf is about the same, beast i don't remember much about character creation. Of course, any splat has extended capabilities, but this freedom to buy more stuff may be enough for the player get the stuff he cares","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26883-imortalkiller","name":"ImortalKiller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-11T18:51:17-07:00","id":1535476,"title":"","content":"Mortal characters are usually, &quot;Prelude&quot;, characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}